{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The weight limit for an elevator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726ceb374a9997197b7c47009e586ebf30a3d9a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1500$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> kilograms. The average weight of the people in the elevator is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kilograms. If the combined weight of the people is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kilograms over the limit, how many people are in the elevator?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8dffa8a7e9d0b5ceaade1e180d246a09bdda6566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 14 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 17 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 16 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the combined weight is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> kilograms over the limit, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726ceb374a9997197b7c47009e586ebf30a3d9a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1500$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> kilograms, the combined weight must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c6078148b2d33d4538440c77910a38167515dd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1500 + 100 = 1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" /> kilograms.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of people in the elevator. Using the known average and the combined weight, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d38fa61ac1097c122b0d6ebd8893f52c813f12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1600}{p} = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"85\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e844857813ae6192c93303b48f7a284507e3972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\frac{1600}{80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/27646c5e907c69d0252e838ef54bc751fa3d53f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•<